dwrite: Synthesize an empty face name when a font has none.

A font whose only subfamily name record (nameID 2) is zero-length ends up
with no face name strings: heap_strdupnW() returns NULL for a zero-length
string, add_localizedstring() rejects it, and opentype_get_font_facename()
returns names == NULL. init_font_data() then passes data->names to
fontstrings_get_en_string(), which calls FindLocaleName() on it and
faults on the NULL object. Any font collection that includes such a font
crashes, e.g. in CreateFontCollectionFromFontSet().

Give such fonts an empty en-us face name and let the existing
differentiation rules add weight, stretch and style terms to it, the same
way they handle a face name with no style terms. A non-regular font gets a
name such as "Light"; a regular one keeps the empty name. Only fonts that
would otherwise have no face name take this path.

Seen with the ABC Favorit Mono Light web font served to EVE Frontier's
in-game browser, which loads it without trouble on Windows.

---
--- a/dlls/dwrite/font.c
+++ b/dlls/dwrite/font.c
@@ -4353,6 +4353,17 @@
     opentype_get_font_metrics(&stream_desc, &data->metrics, NULL);
     opentype_get_font_facename(&stream_desc, props.lf.lfFaceName, &data->names);
 
+    /* Fonts with an empty subfamily name still need a face name; let the rules below derive it. */
+    if (!data->names)
+    {
+        if (FAILED(hr = create_localizedstrings(&data->names))
+                || FAILED(hr = add_localizedstring(data->names, L"en-us", L"")))
+        {
+            release_font_data(data);
+            return hr;
+        }
+    }
+
     if (FAILED(hr = opentype_get_font_familyname(&stream_desc, family_model, &data->family_names)))
     {
         WARN("Unable to get family name from the font file, hr %#lx.\n", hr);
